## Global coding standards

- Follow the primary project style guide in `[coding-style.md](mdc:docs/standards/coding-style.md)`.
- Prefer clear, explicit code over clever one-liners.
- Keep functions and components small and focused.
- Add or update documentation in `docs/` when you introduce non-trivial behavior.

## Error handling & logging

- Use patterns from `[error-handling.md](mdc:docs/standards/error-handling.md)` for consistent error handling.
- Use logging rules from `[logging-standards.md](mdc:docs/standards/logging-standards.md)` for log levels and formats.

## Documentation expectations

- New features should have a folder under `docs/features/` following `[template.md](mdc:docs/features/template.md)`.
- Significant technical decisions should be captured as an ADR in `architecture/ADRs/`.

